SUMMARY:AUTHOR TALK: Colm Tóibín 'The News from Dublin'
DESCRIPTION:For Fans of Brooklyn and Long Island \nJoin the Montclair Literary Festival in welcoming Colm Tóibín\, “one of the world’s best living literary writers” (The Boston Globe)\, on the publication of The News from Dublin\, his brilliant new collection of short stories\, set across Ireland\, Spain\, and America — about the complexities of family\, longing\, loss\, and love. \nYou will not want to miss this event at 3pm on Saturday\, May 2\, 2026\, when the Montclair Literary Festival hosts Colm Tóibín in conversation with Montclair author Garth Risk Hallberg. \nTickets to hear Colm in person are $35 and include a copy of The News from Dublin. Colm will be signing books after the event. \nThe event will be held at the First Congregational Church\, 40 S. Fullerton Avenue\, Montclair. Buy tickets here bit.ly/MLF-Dublin. \nShare this:\n				Share on Facebook (Opens in new window)\n				Facebook\n			\n				Share on Bluesky (Opens in new window)\n				Bluesky\n			\n				Share on LinkedIn (Opens in new window)\n				LinkedIn\n			\n				Share on Threads (Opens in new window)\n				Threads\n			\n				Share on Nextdoor (Opens in new window)\n				Nextdoor\n			\n				Share on WhatsApp (Opens in new window)\n				WhatsApp\n			\n				Email a link to a friend (Opens in new window)\n				Email
