SUMMARY:BOOK WEEK LAUNCH: Tom Perrotta 'Ghost Town'
DESCRIPTION:From bestselling author Tom Perrotta\, hailed by critics as “the Steinbeck of Suburbia” (Time) and “an American Chekhov” (The New York Times)\, comes Ghost Town\, a gripping and darkly nostalgic tale about a tumultuous summer in 1970s suburban New Jersey\, from the perspective of a middle-aged writer looking back on a series of events that changed his life — and the story he finally has the courage to tell \nYou will not want to miss this event at 5:30pm on Saturday\, May 2\, 2026\, when the Montclair Literary Festival and Watchung Booksellers host Tom Perrotta in conversation with renowned musician\, author and producer\, Warren Zanes. \nGhost Town is one of LitHub’s Most Anticipated Books of 2026! \nTickets to hear Tom in person are $35 and include a copy of Ghost Town. Tom will be signing books after the event. \nThe event will be held at the First Congregational Church\, 40 S. Fullerton Avenue\, Montclair. Buy tickets here bit.ly/MLF-Ghost. \nThis event is co-hosted by Festival partner Watchung Booksellers. \nShare this:\n				Share on Facebook (Opens in new window)\n				Facebook\n			\n				Share on Bluesky (Opens in new window)\n				Bluesky\n			\n				Share on LinkedIn (Opens in new window)\n				LinkedIn\n			\n				Share on Threads (Opens in new window)\n				Threads\n			\n				Share on Nextdoor (Opens in new window)\n				Nextdoor\n			\n				Share on WhatsApp (Opens in new window)\n				WhatsApp\n			\n				Email a link to a friend (Opens in new window)\n				Email
